Update API Objects in Place Using kubectl patch > Use strategic merge patch to update a Deployment using the retainKeys strategy > Alternate forms of the kubectl patch command

The `kubectl patch` command takes YAML or JSON. It can take the patch as a file or
directly on the command line.

Create a file named `patch-file.json` that has this content:

```json
{
   "spec": {
      "template": {
         "spec": {
            "containers": [
               {
                  "name": "patch-demo-ctr-2",
                  "image": "redis"
               }
            ]
         }
      }
   }
}
```

The following commands are equivalent:

```shell
kubectl patch deployment patch-demo --patch-file patch-file.yaml
kubectl patch deployment patch-demo --patch 'spec:\n template:\n  spec:\n   containers:\n   - name: patch-demo-ctr-2\n     image: redis'

kubectl patch deployment patch-demo --patch-file patch-file.json
kubectl patch deployment patch-demo --patch '{"spec": {"template": {"spec": {"containers": [{"name": "patch-demo-ctr-2","image": "redis"}]}}}}'
```
